cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use iris in research or in a piece, please cite it."
title: "iris: interactive machine learning for handmade instruments, in one C99 header"
abstract: >-
  iris trains a small neural network on a microcontroller so that a performer
  can demonstrate a handful of gestures paired with sounds and have the mapping
  between them filled in. It is a single C99 header with no dependencies, no
  dynamic allocation and no build system, and it trains on the device rather
  than on a host computer. Behaviour is bit-pinned across compilers and
  optimisation levels so that a saved instrument plays the same way twice.
type: software
authors:
